Z||000003||theogre||04-02-2001||07:52 PM||||Tryx, If you follow that logic,,, then you wouldn't get water on the windshield going thru deep puddles either. Water/mud/etc goes in all directions when you hit it, including ones you would not think posible. The skirts keep allot of crap out of the engine bay.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Tryxalon||04-02-2001||10:12 PM||||Well, not to argue, but it doesn't seem like they would protect as much as trap, at least so to me.  <P>Sounds like it's time for a little scientific experimentation. (muddy road with and without).  We'll see. <P>Thanks for the return guys!! <P>||||reg||5
Z||000005||WKDFIRO||04-03-2001||03:13 AM||||Personal experience talking here....<BR>I had accidently ripped the rubber "curtain" on the pulley side of my V6 while I was working on something else. Not a problem on everyday driving except when it rains hard enough to go through puddles on the freeway or just on the road. Thats when my otherwise tight belts start squealing a little bit. <P>I actually always forget to replace the missing piece unless it rains. So I think I will be taking a little trip to the salvage yard just because of this post!<P>Thanks!||||reg||14
